**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**
Our API is documented by hand but not in a machine readable way so we can't generate documentation or automate penetration testing. This allows us to have rich API documentation instead of the static version we have now, eg: [RapidPro API explorer](https://rapidpro.io/api/v2/explorer/).

**Describe the solution you'd like**
Document our API endpoints in [OpenAPI v3 JSON](https://swagger.io/specification/) format. This could be generated from comments in the API code ([blog](https://dev.to/acanimal/express-api-with-autogenerated-openapi-doc-through-swagger-7na)). I think it'd be better to generate it from comments so the docs are tied to the code.

Once generated it could either be served from the server, or published as a separate artifact. I think it'd be better to serve it from the server so you can see the exact version for the server you're trying to integrate with.

Finally this can be integrated into the docs site with a [Hugo plugin](https://www.tenfourty.com/hugo-oai-swagger-example/) to replace [the docs we have currently](https://docs.communityhealthtoolkit.org/apps/reference/api/).

**Describe alternatives you've considered**
- We could use a different version of OpenAPI than v3 and JSON, or a different spec altogether, but it seems to be the only one that works with our automatic penetration testing framework, so go with that.

