**Describe the issue**

Currently the experience of consuming the `CHTDatasourceService` in webapp is annoying.  Both the `get` and `bind` methods on the service are async and so code must await them before going on to make _another async call_ to get the data they actually want.

```ts
const datasource = await this.chtDatasourceService.get();
const person = await datasource.v1.person.getByUuid(id);

// OR

const getPerson = await this.chtDatasourceService.bind(Person.v1.get);
const person = await getPerson(Qualifier.byUuid(id));
```

It is annoying to have to `await` twice and it really limits the re-usability of the "bound" functions since they cannot be initialized in a the constructor of a consuming class.  

**Describe the improvement you'd like**
Thanks to the wonders of TypeScript and the built-in [Parameters](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/utility-types.html#parameterstype) and [ReturnType](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/utility-types.html#returntypetype) types, it is pretty simple to update the `CHTDatasourceService.bind` method to return a function (not a Promise) that wraps the provided function in a type-safe manner. 

```ts
Person.v1.get
// (context: DataContext) => (qualifier: Readonly<{ uuid: string; }>) => Promise<Nullable<Person. v1.Person>>

const getPerson = chtDatasourceService.bind(Person.v1.get);
// (qualifier: Readonly<{   uuid: string }>) => Promise<Nullable<Person.v1.Person>>

const person = await getPerson(Qualifier.byUuid(id));
// Nullable<Person.v1.Person>
``` 

The wrapper function preserves all the typing from the provided function, but basically delays the async dataContext binding until the function is actually called.

**What feature do you want to improve?**
Currently we support getting a report doc [via cht-datasource](https://docs.communityhealthtoolkit.org/cht-datasource/interfaces/Report.v1.Report.html) and our [REST API](https://docs.communityhealthtoolkit.org/building/reference/api/#getapiv1reportuuid).  However, this report data only includes the minified (dehydrated) data about the report's `contact` lineage.

**Describe the improvement you'd like**

Similar to the `PersonWithLineage`/`PlaceWithLineage`/`ContactWithLineage` APIs, we need a `ReportWithLineage` interface.  The normal report interface should be updated to be (with the new `contact` field):

```ts
  export interface Report extends Doc {
    readonly form: string;
    readonly reported_date: Date;
    readonly fields: DataObject;
    readonly contact?: NormalizedParent;
  }
```

This should not require any changes to the actual implementation code, though, since the minified contact data (that fits the `NormalizedParent` interface) should already be included in the returned report data (it just was not called out on the interface).

Then, we need to add a new interface:

```ts
  export interface ReportWithLineage extends Report {
    readonly contact?: Contact.v1.ContactWithLineage | NormalizedParent;
  }
```

In addition to the interface, we need to add a new `getWithLineage` function to the [`Report.v1` namespace](https://github.com/medic/cht-core/blob/5c1f9ba4a149041dd2a16e58420546731cd27b25/shared-libs/cht-datasource/src/report.ts#L16).  

I am thinking the `local/report.ts` implementation for this function would look something like:

```ts
  /** @internal */
  export const getWithLineage = ({ medicDb, settings }: LocalDataContext) => {
    const getLineageDocs = getLineageDocsById(medicDb);
    const getLineage = getContactLineage(medicDb);

    return async (identifier: UuidQualifier): Promise<Nullable<Report.v1.ReportWithLineage>> => {
      const [report, ...contacts] = await getLineageDocs(identifier.uuid);
      if (!isReport(report, identifier.uuid)) {
        return null;
      }

      if (!isNonEmptyArray(contacts)) {
        logger.debug(`No lineage contacts found for report [${identifier.uuid}].`);
        return report;
      }

      const [baseContact, ...lineageContacts] = contacts;
      if (baseContact && contactTypeUtils.isPerson(settings.getAll(), baseContact)) {
        return {
          ...report,
          contact: isNonEmptyArray(lineageContacts)
            ? await getLineage(lineageContacts, baseContact as Person.v1.Person)
            : baseContact
        };
      }

      return {
        ...report,
        contact: await getLineage(contacts)
      };
    };
  };
```

This _may_ just work with the current implementation in `local/libs/lineage.ts`, but I have not actually tested it yet... 😅 

As with the other cht-datasource functions we will want to update the [api report controller](https://github.com/medic/cht-core/blob/5c1f9ba4a149041dd2a16e58420546731cd27b25/api/src/controllers/report.js#L19) to handle returning the report with lineage when the `with_lineage` query param is true. (This will be used by the remote adapter implementation in cht-datasource.)

Update the exported function to accept `dependencies.dataContext` instead of `dependencies.DB`. Update the consuming code (in other parts of cht-core) to pass in the proper dataContext from cht-datasource instead of the database.  

